In this manner therefore pray: 'Our Father who art in Heaven, may Thy name be kept holy;
28060a0045	let Thy kingdom come; let Thy will be done, as in Heaven so on earth;
28060b0025	give us to-day our bread for the day;
28060c0069	and forgive us our shortcomings, as we also have forgiven those who have failed in their duty towards us;
28060d0043	and bring us not into temptation, but rescue us from the Evil one.'
28060e0056	For if you forgive others their offences, your Heavenly Father will forgive you also;

The eye is the lamp of the body. If then your eyesight is good, your whole body will be well lighted;
280617008c	but if your eyesight is bad, your whole body will be dark. If however the very light within you is darkness, how dense must the darkness be!
28061800de	No man can be the bondservant of two masters; for either he will dislike one and like the other, or he will attach himself to one and think slightingly of the other. You cannot be the bondservants both of God and of gold.

Provide no gold, nor even silver nor copper to carry in your pockets;
280a0a0067	no bag for your journey, nor change of linen, nor shoes, nor stick; for the labourer deserves his food.
280a0b0076	Whatever town or village you enter, inquire for some good man; and make his house your home till you leave the place.

You are blind! Why, which is greater? --the offering, or the altar which makes the offering holy?
2817140045	He who swears by the altar swears both by it and by everything on it;
281715004d	he who swears by the Sanctuary swears both by it and by Him who dwells in it;
2817160059	and he who swears by Heaven swears both by the throne of God and by Him who sits upon it.
2817170129	Alas for you, Scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites, for you pay the tithe on mint, dill, and cumin, while you have neglected the weightier requirements of the Law--just judgement, mercy, and faithful dealing. These things you ought to have done, and yet you ought not to have left the others undone.

then let those who are in Judaea escape to the hills;
